hi I'm Erik Bosse and Avengers infinity  war is finally here and like an eager  little fanboy looking out the window for  Papa to come home boy who I have  feelings I know it's a little early and  maybe you have not seen it yet I was  lucky to see it a little early but do  not worry I'm not gonna spoil anything  this is my non-spoiler review of the  movie really just some deeper thoughts  to consider as you head into the movie  or if you have seen it a hot take to not  along - or shake away okay so how was  Avengers infinity war well answer that  question you have to consider what kind  of movie this is now it's hard to judge  infinity war as a movie because  emotionally speaking this is more of an  event than a movie a crossover finale  paying off a decade of interweaving  storylines across multiple previous  movies now a movie traditionally has  three acts introduced the hero challenge  a hero and then show what the hero does  to overcome those challenges this is  pretty much the formula that we've seen  Marvel Studios do in every one of its  past adventures taking characters and  storylines from comic books and fitting  them into a cinematic format a  redemption tale team-up caper spy  thriller buddy comedy political drama  and breakup story kind of but Infinity  Ward doesn't do that instead it plays  like a true comic book crossover issue  designed to pay off essential back  issues with interesting conflict and  teamwork and surprising pairings  spectacle after spectacle and powerful  emotional gut punches and that thrill is  infinity wars first major strength it is  all third act it's the finale to the  movie that we've been watching for ten  years now it doesn't answer all the  questions there's still another Avengers  4 in the pipeline for that but to use  Game of Thrones season 6 terms it's  definitely a penultimate battle of the  Basterds to a surely forthcoming winds  of winter the closest thing to a  protagonist we get in this movie is  Thanos himself who's the second big  strength Thanos his goal of collecting  the six Infinity stones and wiping out  half the universe is the mission that we  are most curious to see accomplished  even if it breaks our hearts to see that  happen that's how you know you have a  great villain by the way like kill  monger and black panther a part of us  kind of wants to see the evil plan  succeed mostly because we care so much  about all these characters that we want  to see how they respond and that  emotional connection is the third big  strength of infinity war the chemistry  between the characters I pointed out in  my past analyses on this channel that  the secret magic of the superhero  team-up movies is the specific visual of  Hiro's personality and abilities  complementing each other in interesting  ways Thor hammer and cap shield to  create a shockwave ant-man riding Hawk  eyes arrow Groot using his body as a  tree shield to protect the other  guardians the father-son connection  between Tony Stark and Peter Parker as  they stitch and shove together a cleaved  fairy as this whole franchise has  evolved it's less about these  personalities as individual heroes as it  is about the way they set each other up  for spikes and match each other's  strengths this cooperative ensemble  energy is the beating heart of infinity  war it leads to some of the biggest  laughs and yes some of the biggest gasps  both had scene than alley-oop each other  and that the humanity that connects all  of them I truly loved this experience I  was surprised at how a cathartic  infinity war end up being connected me  to all these little moments of joy that  I've experienced over the past 10 years  that said I don't expect everyone who  sees it to feel that way  Avengers infinity war was a gamble by  Marvel Studios it's essentially a  Hollywood version of the ploys that  Marvel comics would use creating these  big crossover events like Marvel Comics  civil war that would invest you in lots  of other character storylines that you  might not otherwise have cared that much  about like you could argue that in the  mid-2000s not a ton of people were  clamoring for a Captain America movie  until the Civil War event in the comics  now he's one of the most beloved  superheroes of Hollywood I would say  that Marvel's gamble appears to have  paid off big time in this movie ever  since Sam Jackson teased this wider  cinematic universe and the post-credits  scene of the first Iron Man most of us  really have bought into watching all  these movies so that we're all pretty  much in on the joke by now but for  anyone who isn't who maybe caught Iron  Man or The Avengers or black panther but  missed all the other movies in between  infinity war might not have the same  emotional effect kind of like a non Game  of Thrones watcher dropping in on battle  of the bastards the pacing of the  visuals and arrows it's all exciting but  you know you're not gonna feel what the  creator's want you to feel namely  satisfaction when a dog bites really  pain in the face so as a standalone  story removed from its own cinematic  history  eventine award doesn't really hold up as  its own arc you could say it's over long  and overcrowded with characters and  spectacle it doesn't  necessarily have the elegance and the  confinement of the genre Bucky and  superhero movies like Logan or the Dark  Knight but it's also not trying to do  what those movies did the Marvel  Cinematic Universe is frenzied and funny  and firework II joyful and Avengers  infinity war is the ultimate summation  of all that contained in one powerful  climax phrasing yeah I know what I said  but I'll throw it over to you guys  if you have seen the movie how do you  think it ranks up against the other MCU  films also if you have seen it just be  cool and don't spoil stuff in the  comments we don't have to block anybody  comment down below with your thoughts or  tweet me directly I da boss and  following the rockstars on Twitter for  updates on our videos like it share this  video subscribe to new rock stars for  all of our deep dives into infinity war  it is infinity week so check out our  breakdowns of some of the scenes that  have been released in advance and be on  the lookout for our panel review in this  week's new rockstars news as well as a  breakdown of the post credits scene and  all the movies Easter eggs and next  week's full movie breakdown thanks for  watching bye  [Music]
 

